<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bungo Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bungo Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, corresponding to most of modern Ōita Prefecture. From the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakura">Kamakura</a> period it was the home base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otomo-clan">Ōtomo clan</a>, whose port town of Funai traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the Portuguese in the 16th century. After the Ōtomo lost it in 1593 it was divided among several small domains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bungo-province.jpg" alt="Bungo Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Bungo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
